n></a><button aria-controls="primary-nav" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open navigation menu" class="mobile-menu" type="button">Menu</button><nav aria-label="Main navigation" class="nav" id="primary-nav"><a href="../../en/index.html">Overview</a><a href="../../en/projects/index.html">Projects</a><a href="../../en/roadmap/index.html">Roadmap</a><a href="../../en/contact/index.html">Contact</a></nav><nav aria-label="Language / Taal" class="language-switch"><a data-language-switch="nl" href="../../projects/fakebank-attack-defend.html" lang="nl">NL</a><a aria-current="true" aria-label="Current language: English" data-language-switch="en" href="../../en/projects/fakebank-attack-defend.html">EN</a></nav><div class="theme-switch" role="group" aria-label="Color theme"><button type="button" class="theme-choice" data-theme-select="dark" aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Dark theme" title="Dark theme"><span aria-hidden="true">☾</span></button><button type="button" class="theme-choice" data-theme-select="light" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Light theme" title="Light theme"><span aria-hidden="true">☼</span></button></div><a aria-label="About Jeroen and contact" class="profile-link" href="../../en/contact/index.html"><img alt="" height="40" src="../../assets/jeroen-portrait.webp" width="40"/><span>Jeroen</span></a></div></div></div><main id="main"><div class="shell"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="../../en/projects/index.html">← All cases</a><span>/</span><span>CTFs</span></div><header class="page-header"><div class="eyebrow">Security case · CTF investigation</div><h1>FakeBank: Attack &amp; Defend</h1><p>An authorized web-security exercise translating offensive observations into proposed defensive controls.</p></header><div class="dossier-meta"><span class="pill completed">Completed</span><span>Nov 2026</span><span>Evidence-based case — no simulated results</span></div><div class="dossier-layout"><div class="dossier-content"><img alt="" class="dossier-art" decoding="async" height="900" loading="eager" src="../../assets/fakebank-art-hd.svg" width="1600"/><p class="dossier-kicker">An authorized web-security exercise translating offensive observations into proposed defensive controls.</p><section><h2>Research question</h2><p>What goes wrong when an unlinked application path is treated as an access-control boundary?</p></section><section><h2>Method and tools</h2><ul><li>Explored the simulated banking application in Firefox within the authorized lab scope.</li><li>Performed permitted directory enumeration with Dirb and discovered a staff-oriented deposit interface.</li><li>Completed the prescribed offensive challenge action and documented the defensive perspective.</li></ul><p class="status-evidence">Tools: TryHackMe · Firefox · Dirb</p></section><section><h2>Observations and evidence</h2><p>TryHackMe accepted the offensive lab answer. Defensive controls were not implemented or independently tested.</p></section><section><h2>Limitations</h2><p>This was a simulation. No real bank vulnerability or effective defensive enforcement is claimed.</p></section><section><h2>What I learned</h2><p>Hidden URLs are not authorization controls. Privileged actions require server-side checks, transaction validation and reliable audit logs.</p></section><section><h2>Next verification step</h2><p>Design an authorized negative test for rejected actions and verify both audit records and account balances.</p></section></div><aside class="dossier-aside"><h2>Evidence status</h2><span class="pill completed">Completed</span><p>TryHackMe accepted the offensive lab answer. Defensive controls were not implemented or independently tested.</p><div class="divider"></div><h3>Next checkpoint</h3><p>Design an authorized negative test for rejected actions and verify both audit records and account balances.</p></aside></div></div></main><noscript><p class="shell">All content is available without JavaScript. JavaScript enables the interactive search and filters.</p></noscript>